    "durationMs": 324789,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified.\n\n**What was built:**\n- Rails 8.0.2 API-only app (generated and dependencies installed in-session) with a `links` table (`code` unique-indexed, `url`, `clicks` default 0) via ActiveRecord on the provided PostgreSQL, configured entirely through `DATABASE_URL`\n- `POST /links` — validates the URL (absolute http/https with host, stored unchanged), validates codes as 4–20 chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`, generates a unique 6-char code when omitted; `201` on success, `409` for duplicate custom codes, `422` for missing/invalid url, invalid code, or malformed JSON (including a fallback for JSON bodies sent without a JSON content-type)\n- `GET /links/{code}` — `200` with `{code, url, clicks}` or `404` JSON error\n- `GET /r/{code}` — atomic `increment_counter` (exactly one click per hit) then `302` with `Location` equal to the stored URL; `404` JSON for unknown codes\n- `GET /links` — `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n}` in ascending creation order\n- `start.sh` — runs `bin/rails db:prepare` (creates/migrates the DB, verified against a fresh database) then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; works from any working directory\n- README section on starting the server\n\n**Notable issue found and fixed:** the bundle resolved `json 3.1.0`, which removed the `quirks_mode` keyword Rails 8.0's ActiveSupport still passes to `JSON.parse`, breaking all JSON bodies with 500s — pinned `json` to `~> 2.9`.\n\n**Verification:** every requirement was exercised with curl across three server restarts — persistence of links and click counts confirmed after restart, duplicate-code races handled via both a pre-check and `RecordNotUnique` rescue, and rubocop reports no offenses. My test server is stopped, so port 8000 is free for `sh start.sh`."
  }
